# Proposed coordinates for the max4 normal-closure certificates

These explicit binary row tables are data, not asserted matrix identities.
`basisRows` is the saved GAP flag basis; `basisInverseRows`, the two transformed
ATLAS outputs, and eleven transformed conjugates of `(x*y²)^6` were computed
from the literal representation. Separate proofs must certify the inverse,
word evaluation and the commutant bound before using them as group facts.

See `source/README.md` for the arithmetic, saved-work provenance and the
Aschbacher–Smith source application. Bit `j` encodes column `j`, exactly as
in `Janko4.Model.Data`.
-/

